            <div xml:id="d72">

                <pb facs="0200" n="106" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg106"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.51/2879</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to J. P. Morgan &amp;
                    Co.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-05-22">May 22, 1930</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sirs</hi>: The receipt is acknowledged of your letter
                    of May 21, 1930, regarding the contemplated issue of bonds of the German
                    Government.</p>
                <p>The Department does not desire to interpose objection to the proposed
                    financing.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. L. Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
